This solution uses a priority queue to explore paths in lexicographical order. It starts by adding all single-cell paths to the queue and then iteratively expands these paths by moving to neighboring cells. The first path of length `k` that is dequeued is guaranteed to be the lexicographically smallest one due to the properties of the priority queue.

